(7164110, 1099423, 102315, '<td valign="top">Your images are always great and I find myself opening all Expert editing challenges just to see if you and Gyaban entered and find your next great creation. You have definitely done it again with this one.<br/> <br/>The only problem with becoming a expert editing fixture on DPC is that people will start to pick apart your images even more because they sense it is yours and want to find the flaws so they have something to critique on. Which is the main point of DPC IMO. That being said I wish the reflection matched. It was the first thing I noticed. Luckily for you it is the one and only flaw.<br/> <br/>I think your score will stay pretty high regardless of the reflection because all together this is a fantastic image. Great work yet again.</td>', 'Your images are always great and I find myself opening all Expert editing challenges just to see if you and Gyaban entered and find your next great creation. You have definitely done it again with this one. The only problem with becoming a expert editing fixture on DPC is that people will start to pick apart your images even more because they sense it is yours and want to find the flaws so they have something to critique on. Which is the main point of DPC IMO. That being said I wish the reflection matched. It was the first thing I noticed. Luckily for you it is the one and only flaw. I think your score will stay pretty high regardless of the reflection because all together this is a fantastic image. Great work yet again.', '2014-01-28 12:49:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(7164114, 1099129, 94815, '<td valign="top">I am enjoying the painterly (or better, printerly) effects like a lithograph and the claustrophobic, dreamlike quality that takes a while to settle on the brain. I wonder if I would have seen the man trolling for sea monsters if not for the title. It still took a few moments which is part of the pleasure in a dynamic piece of art. bump</td>', 'I am enjoying the painterly (or better, printerly) effects like a lithograph and the claustrophobic, dreamlike quality that takes a while to settle on the brain. I wonder if I would have seen the man trolling for sea monsters if not for the title. It still took a few moments which is part of the pleasure in a dynamic piece of art. bump', '2014-01-28 13:01:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(7164213, 1099153, 167332, '<td valign="top">this would be way better without the text.</td>', 'this would be way better without the text.', '2014-01-28 14:59:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(7164215, 1099423, 94815, '<td valign="top">Must be the rejected paramour of the robots, with not unsubtle hints of Miley Cyrus (not to the robots'' taste?). The clean rendering and design suit an album cover. voted earlier</td>', 'Must be the rejected paramour of the robots, with not unsubtle hints of Miley Cyrus (not to the robots'' taste?). The clean rendering and design suit an album cover. voted earlier', '2014-01-28 15:17:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(7164216, 1099330, 94815, '<td valign="top">Bananas are the funniest fruit especially when apprearing unexpectedly where something else makes more sense. Good design and detail. bump</td>', 'Bananas are the funniest fruit especially when apprearing unexpectedly where something else makes more sense. Good design and detail. bump', '2014-01-28 15:23:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(7164218, 1099387, 94815, '<td valign="top">Good name for a band and an appropriate album cover well designed and executed. Love the gas-masked squirrels.</td>', 'Good name for a band and an appropriate album cover well designed and executed. Love the gas-masked squirrels.', '2014-01-28 15:24:57.000000', NULL, 1),
